--TEST--
an `extend` block on a generic `Core` class names each type parameter with a new name: a block of one instance, `Core\ObjectMap<Tag, int>`, and a block with no list are `E0338`, and the help shows the list to write — `rule:classes/an-extend-block-adds-members-to-a-type`
--FILE--
<?nvs
namespace App;

use Core\ObjectMap;
use Core\ObjectSet;

extend ObjectMap<Key, int> as Counts {
    public function total(): uint {
        return $this->count();
    }
}

extend ObjectSet as Tags {
    public function size(): uint {
        return $this->count();
    }
}

echo "unreachable\n";
// covers: lang:classes/extend-blocks
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0338]: this `extend` block does not name the type parameters of `Core\ObjectMap`
  --> %s:7:18
  |
7 | extend ObjectMap<Key, int> as Counts {
  |                  ^^^^^^^^ the type parameters are not named here
  = help: write `extend Core\ObjectMap<K, V> as Name { … }`. Each name in the list is a new name for one type parameter, and a call fills it in from the value's type

error[E0338]: this `extend` block does not name the type parameters of `Core\ObjectSet`
   --> %s:13:8
   |
13 | extend ObjectSet as Tags {
   |        ^^^^^^^^^ the type parameters are not named here
   = help: write `extend Core\ObjectSet<T> as Name { … }`. Each name in the list is a new name for one type parameter, and a call fills it in from the value's type

error: aborting due to 2 errors
%A
